  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conflict, Security and Justice Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SPRING is a 4.5-year, &#xa3;38 million conflict and stability programme, that will work to reduce conflict and support Nigerian communities to better adapt to the effects of climate change. The programme is 15-20% UK International Climate Finance (ICF) eligible. It will support the reduction of rural violence and increased peace, security, justice and climate resilience for citizens in volatile regions of Northern Nigeria. It will focus geographically on Northwest and North Central Nigeria, implementing directly in at least three states, and engaging regionally and nationally to influence scale-up in other states.</narrative>
  </description>
